  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "lapsed_date": "17/10/2025",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (102 (Rev P3); 103 (Rev P3); 104 (Rev P3); 106 (Rev P3); 108 (Rev P3); 109 (Rev P3)  Received:  19 August 2022\r\n001 (Rev P2); 002 (Rev P2); 003 (Rev P2); 004 (Rev P2); 006 (Rev P2); 008 (Rev P2); 009 (Rev P2)  Received:  16 May 2022) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - No additional windows, doors or other glazed openings shall be formed in the single storey rear extension and rear roof dormer extension hereby approved.",
    "Condition : 5 - The developer shall ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to adjoining properties in accordance with the guidance at https://www.london.gov.uk/file/18750/download?token=zV3ZKTpP.  \r\n\r\nAll vehicle arrivals and departures shall be supervised and the condition of the highway examined immediately afterwards.  Any materials shed from the vehicle during such movement shall be immediately removed from the highway, and returned to site or carted away for disposal and shall not be washed into the surface water drainage system.  \r\n\r\nNotes:\r\nIf site staff are instructed by a Council Officer to stop vehicle movements to and from the site if any incidents occur, they must comply with the instructions.  For any further advice, contact the Council's Community Environment Team on 020 8583 5070.",
    "Condition : 6 - No development shall take place until a Construction Method Statement (CMS) relating to the expanded basement hereby approved has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The CMS shall be certified by a qualified professional and give details of excavation, temporary works and construction techniques, including details of potential impacts on neighbouring land based on an assessment of the geology and hydrology of the area. The approved CMS shall be adhered to throughout the construction period for the development.",
    "Condition : 7 - No development shall be carried out until such time as the person(s) undertaking the construction work is a member of the Considerate Constructors Scheme and its code of practice, and the details of their membership and contact details are clearly displayed at the site so that they can be easily read by members of the public.",
    "Condition : 8 - The two front lightwells hereby approved shall be covered with strengthened walk-on glazing or steel railings (both flush and not projecting) only and be permanently retained as such.",
    "Condition : 9 - The dwelling house, as enlarged in accordance with this permission, shall only be used as a single unit of accommodation, and shall not be subdivided, separated or altered in any way so as to create two or more separate units of accommodation, without further grant of planning permission."
  ],
